The dedicated V5 evaluator image was built on the local Docker Desktop Linux engine. Its installed 56-file runtime source map verified successfully during the build and again in a network-disabled, read-only, non-root container. Required evaluator/probe entrypoint imports succeeded. No market evaluation, baseline capture, semantic probe suite, provider call, held-out stage, or replay was run.

Usable immutable reference:

`pit-optimizer-v5-evaluator@sha256:663f1749ba91df9e501e9de705cca83ff1c46305ca5a2ad589380fbe1d9893aa`

This exact reference appears in Docker `RepoDigests` and resolves through both the build context endpoint and the runtime's fixed `npipe:////./pipe/docker_engine` endpoint. It was produced and loaded locally; nothing was pushed to a registry. A mutable convenience tag, `pit-optimizer-v5-evaluator:source-5989471897be`, also exists, but is not the profile authority.

The default resource leaf and `SandboxProfileV5` are contract-valid and authenticated. They establish image/profile preparation only. They are not a baseline authority, evaluator contract, campaign manifest, provider adapter, or approval to evaluate. A later campaign must authenticate and bind the same resources and all remaining data/policy references.

## Environment and non-destructive startup

- Docker CLI 29.7.2 was installed at `C:\Users\llong\AppData\Local\Programs\DockerDesktop\resources\bin\docker.exe`.
- Initial `docker version` returned `Server: null`, and the named pipe `dockerDesktopLinuxEngine` was absent. No Docker Desktop processes initially existed.
- Started `Docker Desktop.exe` using `Start-Process -WindowStyle Hidden` with authorized local escalation. Initial Desktop status query raced startup and returned unavailable; the subsequent engine query succeeded.
- Verified context `desktop-linux` uses the local `npipe:////./pipe/dockerDesktopLinuxEngine` endpoint. `docker buildx ls` showed local `docker` driver, running BuildKit v0.32.2. Every build explicitly selected `--context desktop-linux --builder desktop-linux`.
- Engine: Docker Desktop 4.87.0 (236836), engine 29.7.2, Linux amd64, kernel `6.6.87.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2`, containerd v2.2.5. Image store driver status: `io.containerd.snapshotter.v1`.
- Read-only WSL status/list showed the `docker-desktop` distribution running under WSL 2. No reset, prune, unrelated service stop, global WSL shutdown, virtualization change, or Docker configuration change was performed.
- Sandbox-only Docker access returned access denied for its pipe/buildx lock/log paths. Authorized escalated calls succeeded; no automatic approval rejection occurred.

