## Remaining limitations and source follow-ups

1. Image/profile acquisition has no remaining local engine blocker. Full evaluator/baseline/campaign authorities still need actual data, panel, policy, execution-profile, and identity-transition composition. No runtime performance claim follows from preparation.
2. Do not use the worktree-root Docker build command as an exact-allowlist guarantee without independently reviewing/fixing the observed ignore behavior. The accepted image avoids that dependency by using the verified exact-file context. No source edit was made.
3. The Windows requirements lock omits Linux-only transitive dependencies: this build resolved `SecretStorage==3.5.0` and `jeepney==0.9.0`. The installed versions are recorded in provenance, and the immutable image pins the actual obtained bytes. Fresh rebuild reproducibility requires a separately reviewed Linux-complete lock; no lockfile edit was made. Pinned versions also do not include wheel hashes.
4. Locally loaded RepoDigests do not claim the image is published or recoverable from Docker Hub. Preserve the local image or rebuild from the recorded recipe/context; no registry push was performed.

Final `git status --short --untracked-files=no` was empty. No tracked source change, commit, merge, upload, push, test command, provider/model call, evaluation, baseline capture, held-out stage, or replay was performed. The build recipe's shell `test` statements are file/argument guards, not a test suite.
